  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a digital banking platform called Data Bank, which integrates innovative financial services, cryptocurrency, and data management. Unlike traditional banks, Data Bank operates exclusively online, offering a secure and distributed data storage solution alongside traditional banking operations. The platform is hosted across a network of global nodes, akin to regional branches, providing monetary and data storage services.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- To expand the customer base of Data Bank.\n- To optimize and accurately track customer data storage needs.\n- To develop a robust system for calculating metrics and analyzing data for strategic forecasting and planning.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders: Data Bank management team, investors.\n- Users: Customers of Data Bank, comprising individuals or businesses using banking and secure data storage services.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Customer Data Storage: Allocate cloud storage limits based on account balance.\n- Transaction Management: Handle customer financial transactions with diverse types.\n- Data Distribution: Randomly distribute customers across nodes based on region for enhanced security.\n- Dynamic Node Assignment: Frequently change customer node assignments to prevent unauthorized access.\n- Regional Node Management: Utilize a regions table to manage and assign global nodes.\n- Metric Calculation: Develop tools for assessing growth, data usage, and storage requirements.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Security: Ensure high levels of security in both financial transactions and data storage.\n- Scalability: Support seamless scaling to accommodate growing customer and data demands.\n- Reliability: Maintain consistent system uptime and rapid recovery from potential failures.\n- Performance: Provide efficient data processing and low-latency access across distributed nodes.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0197\nCREATE TABLE `regions` (\n  `region_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `region_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`region_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `nodes` (\n  `node_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `region_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `node_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`node_id`),\n  KEY `nodes_ibfk_1` (`region_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `nodes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`region_id`) REFERENCES `regions` (`region_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `region_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `account_balance` decimal(15,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0.00',\n  `storage_limit_mb` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT '0',\n  `node_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `customers_ibfk_1` (`region_id`),\n  KEY `customers_ibfk_2` (`node_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`region_id`) REFERENCES `regions` (`region_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `customers_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`node_id`) REFERENCES `nodes` (`node_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `transactions` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(15,2) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  KEY `transactions_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `transactions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer_nodes` (\n  `customer_node_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `node_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assigned_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `unassigned_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_node_id`),\n  KEY `customer_nodes_ibfk_1` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `customer_nodes_ibfk_2` (`node_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_nodes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_nodes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`node_id`) REFERENCES `nodes` (`node_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `metrics` (\n  `metric_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `metric_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `metric_value` decimal(18,4) NOT NULL,\n  `calculated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`metric_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
